    "body": "Problem: The msg_ruler event only carries the last highlight group stacked with %$ in 'rulerformat', so ui2 does not apply the earlier highlights.\n\nSolution: Emit a hidden highlight group that combines the stacked groups. It is named after them and is not listed or found by name.\n\nFixes #42014\n\nEach distinct stack gets a group named by joining its member names with '+' (e.g. User1+User2). Groups are reused by member IDs and remain accessible by ID, but are excluded from listings, completion, and contains= matching.\n\nStacks are limited to `MAX_HL_STACK (10)` to avoid dynamic allocation during redraw. Larger stacks fall back to the last group. Unlike ui1, which combines groups as it parses the format, processing stacks incrementally in ui2 could create groups for unused prefixes. For example, `%$B$%$C$x` would require an intermediate group that is never used. Practically the cap will not be touched.",
    "closed_at": null,
